        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.886,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Archimedes did a ‘thought experiment’; he asked himself what happens if the number of sides of the regular polygon gets larger and larger. Working out the details, he arrived at the result "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "A = \\pi \\mathbf { r } ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.179,
            0.886,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here perhaps is the most visual and easy-to-understand explanation for why the area of a circle of radius r has area "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\pi } r ^ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This beautiful visual explanation for the area of the circle was first discovered by Nīlakaṇṭha Somayājī (c. 1500) in his commentary on the Āryabhaṭīya:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
